# The base set: the kits every build's root is made of (the C library, the compiler, a shell, the usual tools). Their
# recipes need each other in a circle, so kit-set.sh leaves them out and build/kits/bootstrap.sh builds them, in
# stages (docs/RECIPES.md, "The bootstrap"). One name per line, in the order of the first stage: each is laid over the
# stand-in system (recipes/bootstrap) as soon as it is built, so a line's recipe is built with the lines above it.
linux-headers
zlib
xz
m4
bison
python3
glibc
gmp
mpfr
mpc
binutils
gcc
make
bash
perl
coreutils
sed
grep
gawk
findutils
diffutils
tar
gzip
patch
